 "details": {
  "title": "Arban – Ornament Study No. 79",
  "lead": "From Arban's Grande méthode complète de cornet à pistons et de saxhorn, first edition, 1864. The notes are the cornet part as printed, in written pitch for the B♭ cornet. Below: the book's own words, translated from the French.",
  "facts": [
   [
    "Book",
    "Arban, Grande méthode complète de cornet à pistons et de saxhorn, first edition (Paris: Léon Escudier, 1864)"
   ],
   [
    "Section",
    "Ornaments"
   ],
   [
    "Page in the book",
    "118–119"
   ],
   [
    "Layout",
    "Each trill begins with three small notes and closes with two, and is followed by a single note: one trilled note to each line of the book, with the single notes stepping down under it. The book prints no tempo for this study. The book prints the valves under the small notes in some bars; they hold for the trill: F sharp with 1 2 3, G with 1 3 and A with 3 in bars 25 to 31 and 73, and E with 1 2 in bars 65 and 67."
   ]
  ],
  "sections": [
   {
    "heading": "The trill",
    "paragraphs": [
     "On valve instruments the trill is the hardest of all the ornaments. Only the half-step trill is really bearable. Whole-step trills can be made, but take care to press the valves down evenly, so that each beat is quite distinct.",
     "So first work patiently, and without hurrying, at studies Nos. 60 to 67, until each sound comes out cleanly. Later you can play the studies on the trill, following the fingerings shown exactly. (See Nos. 68 to 80.)"
    ]
   },
   {
    "heading": "A word on all of these",
    "paragraphs": [
     "Since all the lessons on ornaments were written to serve as studies, I have brought together, on purpose and in abundance, every kind of ornament. But take great care not to overuse them so in practice, for that would be in the worst of taste."
    ]
   }
  ],
  "sources": [
   {
    "title": "IMSLP: Grande méthode complète de cornet à pistons (Arban), first edition, Paris 1864",
    "url": "https://imslp.org/wiki/Grande_m%C3%A9thode_compl%C3%A8te_de_cornet_%C3%A0_pistons_(Arban,_Jean-Baptiste)"
   }
  ]
 }
